    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nI. $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{2} + 2 e^{2 x + y},\\,\\frac{3 x}{2} + e^{2 x + y}⟩$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=⟨5 y^{4} - \\frac{y}{2},\\,20 x y^{3} + \\frac{x}{2}⟩$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=⟨5 y e^{2 x},\\,x - 5 e^{2 x}⟩$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I gives the required area. In this case,\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2 e^{2 x + y} + \\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2 e^{2 x + y} + \\frac{3}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\left(2 e^{2 x + y} + \\frac{3}{2}\\right)-\\left(2 e^{2 x + y} + \\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)+\\left(2 e^{2 x + y}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\left(2 e^{2 x + y}\\right)=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=20 y^{3} - \\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=20 y^{3} + \\frac{1}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\left(20 y^{3} + \\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\left(20 y^{3} - \\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(20 y^{3}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\left(20 y^{3}\\right)=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=5 e^{2 x}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1 - 10 e^{2 x},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\left(1 - 10 e^{2 x}\\right)-\\left(5 e^{2 x}\\right)=\\left(1\\right)+\\left(- 10 e^{2 x}\\right)-\\left(5 e^{2 x}\\right)=1 - 15 e^{2 x}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
